OL,3,GUK long range forecast                 
OL,5,COutlook for Fri 27 Nov to Sun 6 Dec    
OL,6,FThrough the rest of November and into  
OL,7,Fearly December, the UK will remain     
OL,8,Funder the competing influence of high  
OL,9,Fpressure extending across the country  
OL,10,Ffrom the northeast and Atlantic        
OL,11,Fweather systems attempting to arrive   
OL,12,Ffrom the west or southwest at times.   
OL,13,FWestern and southwestern parts of the  
OL,14,FUK are likely to see the most frequent 
OL,15,Fand heaviest spells of rain.           
OL,16,FConditions in the north and east are   
OL,17,Flikely to be drier though still with   
OL,18,Fsome rain at times. This pattern means 
OL,19,Ftemperatures will often be below       
OL,20,Faverage with any milder interludes     
OL,21,Fmost probable in the southwest. Snow   
OL,22,Fis also likely at times across parts   
OL,23,Fof the UK, most likely over northernice
OL,24,Fhills but there is a greater chanceg TV
